 recommendation:'Ship pairing A (Bricolage Grotesque + Figtree). It is the only one that is both friendly and precise: the headings have personality that suits a general audience and the arcade game, the body text is the most relaxed to read on the dark navy, and three files total 117,972 bytes (97,044 without the optional italic), well under the 250 KB budget. Use tabular-nums on every numeric readout. Runner-up is B if a more bookish, editorial tone is wanted; C is best kept as an idea for the game HUD only (Oxanium alone is 14,044 bytes and could be added to A for score and readout digits while staying under budget: 132,016 bytes total).',
 notes:[
  'Method: licence, weights and variable flag read from https://api.fontsource.org/v1/fonts/<id> (all six report OFL-1.1, latin subset, variable: true); axes from https://api.fontsource.org/v1/variable/<id>. Every file was downloaded with curl on 2026-11-18, HTTP 200, first four bytes wOF2; bytes are the sizes on disk.',
  'URLs are pinned to the version the API reported (5.3.0, or 5.3.1 for Source Sans 3). The pinned files were compared byte-for-byte with the @latest files and are identical today. The specimens load the copies in the dl folder.',
  'licenseUrl points to the LICENSE text in the fontsource/font-files repository (fetched, each begins with the project copyright line and the SIL Open Font License 1.1 statement). The path https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/fontsource/fonts/<id>@latest/LICENSE does NOT return a licence (it returns a proxy notice), so do not link it. OFL requires shipping the copyright notice and licence text with the fonts: copy each LICENSE file next to the woff2 files.',
  'Tabular figures were checked in headless Chrome by measuring 1111, 0000 and 7777 at 40px with and without font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums. Bricolage Grotesque and Figtree: proportional by default, equal with tnum. Source Sans 3, IBM Plex Sans, Oxanium: equal by default. Fraunces: unequal in both cases.',
  'Use the real minus sign (U+2212) in "-1000 HU"; it is present in all three body fonts and matches the digit width better than a hyphen. The middle dot (U+00B7) is present in all families.',
  'Doubt: Fontsource file names for extra axes (latin-opsz-normal, latin-full-normal) are not listed by the fonts API; they were found by trying the URL. bricolage-grotesque latin-full-normal.woff2 returned 404, latin-opsz-normal.woff2 returned 200.',
  'Use font-display: swap in production (specimens use block so screenshots never show the fallback). Only the latin subset was tested; characters outside it (for example Greek beta or gamma, superscript digits beyond 1-3) would fall back to the system font, so check any such glyphs the copy needs or write them as words/markup (<sup>18</sup>F).'
 ]};
fs.mkdirSync(OUT,{recursive:true});
fs.writeFileSync(path.join(OUT,'fonts.json'),JSON.stringify(j,null,2)+'\n');
const back=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(OUT,'fonts.json'),'utf8'));
console.log('parsed ok',back.pairings.map(p=>p.name+' '+p.totalBytes).join(' | '));
EOF
